          "event_id": "run-35082344419-review-compatibility",
          "findings": [
            {
              "evidence": "RemoveDocId now requires the declared MemberMapper.DataType to be assignable from ObjectId, even though BsonMapper exposes registered type conversion and ResolveMember can replace MemberMapper.Setter. I ran the same custom Token ID mapping against the exact base and candidate: the mapping serializes an empty Token as BSON null and its configured setter converts a generated ObjectId back to Token. Base bbb0253 succeeded with `returned=ObjectId stored=ObjectId` and a nonempty copied-back Token; candidate cef2fd rejected it before write with LiteException 214, `Data type Token is not assignable from data type LiteDB.ObjectId`, and count 0. Thus a previously valid custom mapper/member configuration can no longer insert, contrary to the frozen requirement to reject only unsupported generated-value/member-type combinations. The same gate is reached by Insert, Insert(IEnumerable), InsertBulk, and Upsert through the shared GetBsonDocs/RemoveDocId helpers.",
